# Bottom Navigation Layout Rules

Locked files: `src/components/BottomNav.tsx`, rendered once as a **direct child of `<body>`** in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Do not add a second nav in pages. Do not wrap it in `<main>`, flex shells, or page layouts.

- Do NOT `position: fixed` on `html`. Do NOT make `body` a flex column.
- The outer `<nav>` stays `fixed bottom-0 left-0 right-0 z-50 h-[52px] w-full bg-background border-t border-border/30`.
- Inner wrapper stays `flex h-[52px] w-full items-center justify-around px-2 pb-0`.
- Do NOT add `pb-[env(safe-area-inset-bottom)]`, `pb-safe`, `mb-safe`, extra nav height, or negative `bottom` on the nav or its inner wrappers.
- Do NOT `transform` or hide the nav on scroll or route change.

Every route uses `PageShell` with `w-full min-h-full pb-[70px] pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)] bg-background`.
Do not add a second `pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)]` on pages.
`PageHeader` is not sticky.
